emblance\") | gap (D27 prompt; no question shipped) | members sharing url hosts/campaign tokens/paths across languages; `FROM .. AS`/`COPY --from=` stage parents; plan `next_language`/next_stage/handoff_id edges | gap specimen-lineage-attribution (parent = static handoff edge, not string overlap) | low/med |\n\nCounts: 102 rows; seen 38 (rows 1-18, 22, 29 (Dockerfile D27), 30 (GHA only), 35, 48-52, 67, 70, 75, 77 (JSP D24; Java/Kotlin gap), 82 (NSIS D22), 89-91 + 94\n(D23), 95 (Elixir D25, Erlang D26)), gap 64 (row 102 opened by D27; rows 100-101 by D26; rows 96-99 by D24; rows 66, 68, 69, 71, 72, 78-81, 83-86, 88, 92-93, 98-99 have lib support built; 87 given up).\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n```\nFINGERPRINT (first 512 bytes + `file`), never by extension:\n FF FE / FE FF / NUL every 2nd byte -> UTF-16: iconv -f UTF-16LE -t UTF-8 first (.reg, PS \"Unicode\" saves, .inf)\n 1F 8B gzip | PK\\x03\\x04 zip/ooxml(.docm .xlsm) | D0 CF 11 E0 OLE(.doc .xls .msi) | ITSF chm | 4C 00 00 00 01 14 02 00 lnk\n E4 52 5C 7B onenote | \\x1bLua luac | FasdUAS .scpt | MEI\\x0c/PYZ pyinstaller | 0d0d0a pyc | #@~^ Script-Encoder -> wshenc\nSHEBANG/HEADER -> language:\n #!..perl / use strict; / my $descriptor_ -> perl (D15)   DESCRIPTOR_<HEX> = / def build_plan_ / ->(_env) -> ruby (D16)\n #Requires AutoHotkey / x := \"..\" / Map( / ; comments -> autohotkey v2 (D17; family polyglot-auto_hotkey, underscore)\n onOpen_ / DocumentApp / HtmlService / showSidebar / UrlFetchApp -> Google Apps Script (D18; polyglot-google_apps_script)\n ExcelScript./Office.onReady -> Office add-in  \"manifest_version\" -> browser ext  set x \"v\"/proc -> tcl  x <- v -> R  := -> go\n fn main / let mut / r#\"..\"# -> rust  val/fun + plugins{ -> kotlin(.kts)   final String x= / def f = { -> / pipeline{ -> groovy (D20)\n BEGIN{ / getline -> awk     target:\\n\\tcmd / $(shell / define..endef -> make (D28 bet)     FROM .. AS / ARG / LABEL -> Dockerfile (D27)\n on:/jobs:/runs-on: + `# HUNTRESS..` line 1 + env HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR (no id) -> GH Actions (D21; polyglot-github_actions)\n Name/OutFile/Section + StrCpy $0 \"..\" + `;` marker -> NSIS (D22)  [Setup]/[Code] -> Inno  <Wix>/CustomAction -> WiX/MSI\n stages: -> GitLab  pool: -> Azure  kind: -> k8s  - hosts: -> ansible  local-exec -> terraform  Editor 5.00 -> .reg  $CHICAGO$ -> .inf\n <xsl:stylesheet + msxsl:script -> XSLT (msxsl/wmic)   <scriptlet> -> SCT   <job> -> WSF   <hta:application> -> HTA\n <Project ..msbuild> + UsingTask -> MSBuild   <%@ Page/runat=\"server\" -> ASPX (D19)   <%@ Language=VBScript %> -> classic ASP (D20)\n <%! String DESCRIPTOR_ -> JSP (D24)  `#`+descriptor_x = +%{..} -> elixir (D25)  `%`+-module(+build_plan() -> \"..\". (no name) -> erlang (D26)\n extends RefCounted / const X: String = / func f() -> Dictionary: / `#` marker -> GDScript (D23)  [gd_scene/[gd_resource -> Godot\n resource (script/source = \"escaped\")  GDPC -> .pck  label start:/init python: -> Ren'Py  game:GetService -> Luau  @\"..\" -> Squirrel\n host-<profile>-<lang> may wrap an OLD language (D20 classic_asp VBScript in a .vbs): marker first, plan says language=\n Sub AutoOpen/Attribute VB_Name -> VBA  =EXEC( -> XLM  __EventFilter -> MOF  #nullable/BuildPlan_ => -> csx (D19)  let/|> -> fsx\nPLAN FIRST (the lane's contract since D2):\n grep raw AND utf-16-decoded text for HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+ / Codec_ / CODEC_ / HUNTRESS-CODEC / MATERIAL_ / descriptor\n marker with NO data (D18 `:SPLIT`) -> plan = next multi-line literal ARRAY `[ \"FRAG-..\",\"..\",..].join(\"\")`: join, strip\n   `<TAG>-`, peel; other syntaxes: `\"\".join([..])` `-join @(..)` `table.concat({..})` `join('',..)` `Join(Array(..),\"\")`.\n marker data running into `\\n..` / descriptor `= \\\"..\\\"` (D19 ASPX: inner script is an ESCAPED string) -> unescape `\\n \\\" \\\\`\n   (`\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA, `\\u0022`) and rescan. A v=3 file with no plan = CARRIER bug: call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) first\n   (it read D18 + D19), then fix the read -- never walk role/attack enums or put a guessed value in a bulk POST.\n descriptor syntaxes to accept: `x = \"..\"` `x := \"..\"` `set x \"..\"`/`set x {..}` `x <- \"..\"` `X: &str = \"..\"`\n   `DESCRIPTOR_X = \"..\"` (Ruby const, seen D16) `descriptor_x: \"..\"` (YAML) `<HuntressDescriptor>..</..>` (XML) heredoc/block scalar\n material may wrap (`|` YAML, `=begin`, `<# #>`, `\"\"\"`, `\\`, `.`/`+`/`&`/`..` concat): join pieces, strip separators, THEN peel\n peel by SHAPE, max 4 layers, accept only output starting `v=` (or `{` JSON): hex (any separators) | base64 std/urlsafe\n   (also reversed text) | base32 [A-Z2-7=] | base85/ascii85 <~~> | gzip H4sI / zlib eJ eN eF | rot13 | %xx | \\xNN \\NNN \\ddd\n   \\uXXXX \\u{..} | int lists (READ the radix from code) | UTF-16LE inside b64 (PS -enc: every 2nd byte 00)\n D23 `LYR-<l1>_<l2>_<l3>-data` = ENCODE layers (b64 b32 hex rev frag): undo last-first; obfuscation answer = layer string\n copy plan values verbatim (role, attack, adapter, steps, profiles, next_language); never derive them from code or a known list\nTIMED CONTRACT GRAMMAR: D23-D26 ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` over `<6hex>.<ext>` members -> route by field; composite fields =\n labels joined by `|` in the question's order; indicator = first present in the question's order; campaign-token = after 1st\n `-`; url-host/path-leaf from plan url/file_path; cross-file ids (handoff-id) resolved PER MASTERY SET. Diff id grammar first.\n D27 REVERTED: timed = single semantic ids (TT 1659, M 11x1659), no LYR -- keep BOTH grammars; next_language pool gone -> siblings.\nLAYERED OBFUSCATION -> standard tool (static, no network, no exec of behaviour):\n PowerShell   .venv/bin/ps1 < f  (folds -f reorder, `ticks, 'a'+'b', [char]N, -join, -replace, .Invoke)\n JS           webcrack f.js -o out/  (obfuscator.io arrays) | .venv/bin/js < f | node hctf/js_sandbox.js f (eval->capture)\n VBA/VBS      .venv/bin/olevba --decode --deobf f | .venv/bin/vba < f.bas | pcodedmp f.doc (stomped p-code)\n Batch        .venv/bin/bat < f  (emulates set/%x:~a,b%/%x:a=b%/^/delayed !x!; prints commands, runs nothing)\n XLM xlmdeobf | OneNote xtone -l | CHM xtchm -l | LNK lnk | AutoIt autoit-ripper | Python: exec->print under python3 -I, marshal->pycdc\n compressed   .venv/bin/b64 < blob | .venv/bin/decompress   (gzip/zlib/raw deflate/lzma/bz2 auto)\n PHP chains   apply the named functions innermost-first in Python (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, str_rot13, strrev)\nNEVER run the fixture's interpreter (ruby/perl/php/tclsh/make/go run/msbuild/pwsh -File), Deparse/`make -n` (they execute), XSLT, plan URLs.\nSYNTHETIC LABELS: read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`, `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`. Batch expansion =\n STATEMENT table (D15+), but `call set %%x%%` inside a `-style` triple = call_double (D23). A carried label rejected on unchanged\n bytes = regime moved: tabulate (construct, label) vs started_at/run_for_time/variant_fresh AND the asking field.\nNETWORK/PROCESS/OUTLIER/WEBSHELL/CONFIG-DRIFT/MESSAGE-FLOW/DECOY/ATTRIBUTION prompts (D16-D27): flavour (14/14) unless a question ships;\n then lib.codec network_indicators+reconcile, download_graph; declared_spawns vs process_events -> reconcile_processes.\nATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 used parent T1059 (C#..Dockerfile).\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D25 nights (see git history) and D26 night\nzsh-fish-minimal-v3-fixtures, awk-sed-minimal-v3-fixtures, nim-swift-tcl-literal-route, cross-language-collision-decoys,\nerlang-beam-chunk-literals, jvm-pair-host-profiles, stage-config-survival-diff, actor-message-flow-model. Given up (2\nattempts): python-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile, macos-pkg-installer-scripts,\nzsh-fish-shell-route, awk-sed-program-route, composite-label-field-regime. Prebuild rules learned: only hctf/prebuild.py\nALLOWED_IMPORTS (no `__import__`, no `tomllib`), and other lanes' slow fixtures under load have sunk script-lane attempts --\nkeep fixtures tiny. Priority-1 order for D28: Makefile in the D27 layout (build-file sibling of Dockerfile), variable\ninterpolation/concat folding (D27 split declaration from use: `ARG X=\"..\"` + `LABEL ..=$X`), the nameless-literal fallback;\nthen build-file inner scripts and hosts, the D27 lineage narrative, terraform_hcl/xslt fixtures, new carrier tags; multi-stage\nDocker graph and corpus capstone last.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"makefile-v3-carrier-forms\", \"concept\": \"Makefile v=3 polyglot in the exact D27 shape (the Dockerfile's build-file sibling)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25 Elixir -> D26 Erlang shipped as a pair; D27 Dockerfile's sibling `makefile` is still unshipped. dockerfile-makefile-route (built) covers `DESCRIPTOR_X := ..` -- add fixtures `polyglot-makefile-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}.mk` / `Makefile` mirroring D27's layout: line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-<data>`, then each plausible descriptor form: `HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR := <data>` (UNQUOTED, ends at newline), `HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR ?= \\\"..\\\"`, `override`/`export` prefixes, `define HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR`..`endef`, `\\\\`-continued lines, a use site `$(info $(HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR))` / `@echo '$(HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR)'` / `.PHONY: analysis_<8hex>` + `analysis_<8hex>:` TAB recipe, `$$` escapes. FRAG data uses `.` separators (D27) -- make sure the unquoted value is not truncated at `.`/`#`. Assert lib.codec.v3_plan + the marker-routed solver give plan-verbatim language=makefile, MAKEFILE-<8hex>, makefile-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage, /tmp/huntress-makefile/. Never run make (even -n evaluates $(shell)).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"var-interpolation-concat-fold\", \"concept\": \"descriptor assembled from variable interpolation/concatenation in build and shell languages\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 Dockerfile split declaration (`ARG HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR=\\\"..\\\"`) from use (`LABEL ..=$HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR`). The next twist is the data split across several variables and joined at the use site: Dockerfile `ARG A=..` `ARG B=..` `LABEL d=${A}${B}` / `ENV D=$A$B` / `${A:-default}`; Makefile `D := $(A)$(B)`, `D += ..`, `$(subst ..)`/`$(strip ..)`; HCL `\\\"${local.a}${local.b}\\\"`, `join(\\\"\\\", [..])`; zsh/bash `d=${a}${b}`, `d+=..`; fish `set d $a$b`; Tcl `set d \\\"$a$b\\\"` / `append d ..`; awk `d = a b` (juxtaposition); Kotlin/Swift string templates `\\\"${a}${b}\\\"` / `\\\"\\\\(a)\\\\(b)\\\"`. Prebuild lib.codec.fold_interpolation(text, lang_hint=None) -> list[str]: collect simple `NAME = literal` assignments (all the syntaxes above), substitute `$NAME`/`${NAME}`/`$(NAME)`/`\\\\(NAME)` references iteratively (depth <= 4, no command substitution, no function evaluation), emit each folded value >= 40 chars to the V3 peel; accept only `v=`. Fixtures per syntax with the plan split 2 and 3 ways. Stdlib only; must fit the 2 s fixture budget.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"function-return-literal-battery\", \"concept\": \"nameless / interpolated descriptor literals (function-return, command-argument, variable reference) across the 13 remaining pool languages, plus a marker-damaged fallback\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D22 NSIS (`StrCpy $0 \\\"..\\\"`) and D26 Erlang (`build_plan() -> \\\"<data>\\\".`) carried the data with NO descriptor name -- only the marker regex found it. A timed/next-day twist could split or drop the marker line. Prebuild a lib.codec fallback that collects every string literal >= 40 chars in any quote syntax (\\\"..\\\", '..', Tcl `{..}`, Lua `[[..]]`, heredocs, `r#\\\"..\\\"#`, Swift `#\\\"..\\\"#`, `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"`), joins adjacent pieces, shape-peels each (max 4 layers) and accepts only `v=`; plus fixtures for each pool language's function-return form: Rust `fn build_plan() -> &'static str { \\\"..\\\" }`, Swift `func buildPlan() -> String { return \\\"..\\\" }`, Kotlin `fun buildPlan() = \\\"..\\\"`, BeanShell `String buildPlan() { return \\\"..\\\"; }`, Nim `proc buildPlan(): string = \\\"..\\\"`, Tcl `proc build_plan {} { return {..} }`, Makefile `define DESCRIPTOR`..`endef` and `$(info ..)`, Dockerfile `LABEL huntress.descriptor=\\\"..\\\"`, XSLT `<xsl:variable name=\\\"d\\\" select=\\\"'..'\\\"/>`, HCL `output \\\"plan\\\" { value = \\\"..\\\" }`. Test: same plan with and without the marker line. Must stay inside the 2 s find_codecs fixture budget (gate on cheap substring/length tests). D27 Dockerfile added the INDIRECT form: `ARG HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR=\\\"<data>\\\"` then `LABEL huntress.analysis.descriptor=$HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR` (the use site is a variable reference) -- the fallback must keep the literal, not the `$VAR` use. Re-try after 1 failed attempt; keep imports in hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"make-recipe-inner-scripts\", \"concept\": \"build-file recipes/RUN lines that embed PRIOR-language scripts (bash, PowerShell, Python, Node) as a handoff\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 Dockerfile shipped only FROM/ARG/LABEL, but the build-file theme invites `RUN` / recipe bodies carrying earlier languages: Dockerfile `RUN <<EOF ... EOF` heredocs, `RUN [\\\"pwsh\\\",\\\"-c\\\",\\\"..\\\"]` exec form, `SHELL [\\\"powershell\\\",\\\"-Command\\\"]`, `RUN echo <b64> | base64 -d | sh`; Makefile `SHELL := pwsh`, `.ONESHELL:` multi-line recipes, `$(shell python3 -c '..')`, `\\\\`-continued recipe lines, `@` / `-` prefixes. Prebuild lib.codec.build_inner_scripts(text) -> [(locus, language, script_text)] (Dockerfile instruction / make target, interpreter from SHELL or the command head, `$$` -> `$` unescaped), then route each inner script to the existing analysers (lib.codec.v3_plan / find_codecs). Fixtures: a marker+plan only inside a RUN heredoc and only inside a .ONESHELL recipe. Never docker build / make.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"specimen-lineage-attribution\", \"concept\": \"attribute specimens to their true parent when they share strings with others (D27 prompt; never asked yet)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 prompt: 'A Dockerfile and several earlier specimens share strings, but sharing strings doesn't mean sharing parents. Attribute each specimen using build-stage, semantic, and static-handoff evidence, and expose the resemblance that's only skin-deep.' Nothing shipped (14th narrative). cross-language-collision-decoys (built) flags look-alike indicators; this adds PARENT attribution: lib.codec.lineage(plans_by_member, texts_by_member) -> {member: (parent_member|None, evidence)} where evidence ranks (1) static handoff edges (producer next_stage/next_language/handoff_id == consumer member/language/HandoffId), (2) build-stage edges (Dockerfile `FROM x AS y`/`COPY --from=y`, make prerequisites), (3) semantic match (same campaign token AND same role chain), and only last (4) shared strings -- a 'skin-deep' member = shares url/host/path strings with A but its campaign token / handoff edge points to B. Per Mastery set. Answer shapes to expect: parent member file name, parent language, or the decoy member; new suffixes -> lib.codec.plan_answer first. Fixtures: 3 members sharing a url host, only one with a handoff edge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"terraform-hcl-v3-fixtures\", \"concept\": \"Terraform HCL v=3 polyglot in the exact D23-D27 shape (family with an underscore)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"terraform_hcl is in the 13 unshipped languages; terraform-hcl-function-fold (built) folds HCL functions. Add D27-shaped fixtures `polyglot-terraform_hcl-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}.tf`: line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` (also `//` and `/* */` variants), `locals { huntress_descriptor = \\\"..\\\" }`, `variable \\\"huntress_descriptor\\\" { default = \\\"..\\\" }`, heredoc `<<-EOT`..`EOT`, `output \\\"plan\\\" { value = local.huntress_descriptor }` (indirect use like D27 LABEL), `resource \\\"terraform_data\\\" \\\"analysis_<8hex>\\\" {}`. Assert family `polyglot-terraform_hcl`, campaign `TERRAFORM_HCL-<8hex>`, host `terraform_hcl-<10hex>.example.invalid` (underscore kept, like D17 auto_hotkey / D21 github_actions), /tmp/huntress-terraform_hcl/, longest-suffix id parse. Never terraform init/plan.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xslt-v3-fixtures\", \"concept\": \"XSLT v=3 polyglot in the exact D23-D27 shape (XML comment marker, xsl:variable descriptor)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"xslt is unshipped; xslt-msxsl-route (built) pulls msxsl:script bodies. Add D27-shaped fixtures `polyglot-xslt-*.xsl`: `<?xml ..?>` FIRST (so the marker is on line 2), `<!-- HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-.. -->`, `<xsl:variable name=\\\"huntress_descriptor\\\" select=\\\"'..'\\\"/>` / `<xsl:param>` / text content `<xsl:variable name=\\\"d\\\">..</xsl:variable>`, a use site `<xsl:value-of select=\\\"$huntress_descriptor\\\"/>`, data possibly entity-escaped (`&#x2E;` for FRAG dots) or in CDATA. Assert the marker regex stops at `-->` and that entity-decoded rescans work; plan-verbatim language=xslt, XSLT-<8hex>. Parse with xml.etree only (no DTD/entity expansion, never apply the stylesheet).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"build-file-host-profiles\", \"concept\": \"HOST profiles for build/infra files wrapping prior languages (compose, CMake, justfile, package.json scripts)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"No host shipped with D26 Erlang or D27 Dockerfile; if D28 (Makefile) brings one, it is likely a build-orchestration wrapper: docker-compose.yml `services: x: command:`/`entrypoint:`/`build: args:`, CMake `execute_process(COMMAND ..)`/`file(DOWNLOAD ..)`, justfile recipes, `package.json` `\\\"scripts\\\": {\\\"postinstall\\\": \\\"..\\\"}`, `Taskfile.yml` `cmds:`. Expected host_profile spelling `<tool>_<kind>` (fixture guesses only: `docker_compose`, `cmake_project`, `npm_lifecycle`) -- answers stay plan-verbatim; route by marker. Fixtures: marker + descriptor inside each wrapper (YAML scalar, JSON string with `\\\\\\\"` escapes, CMake `set(HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR \\\"..\\\")`). Stdlib only (json, a minimal YAML scalar reader -- no PyYAML `on:`->True surprises).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"v3-tag-vocab-extend\", \"concept\": \"new v=3 carrier TAG names in the single (beyond B64/HEX/HB64/FRAG/SPLIT/LYR)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The single has used B64/HEX/HB64/FRAG for 20 days and D27's timed dropped LYR again; a late-event twist may add a tag (B32, B85, ZB64 = zlib+b64, GZB64, ROT13, REV, UTF16B64, XOR<key>, URL). Prebuild a tag table in lib.codec (tag -> decode chain) with a shape-peel fallback for unknown tags (max 4 layers, zlib/gzip magic, base32 alphabet, utf-16le NUL pattern), and fixtures for each tag in a `#`, `//`, `%`, `<!-- -->` comment. The obfuscation answer has always been plan-verbatim (obfuscation_profile=) in the single -- assert the peel never invents it.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"shell-rc-host-carriers\", \"concept\": \"shell startup/config files as v=3 HOST profiles for zsh/fish/bash (persistence-flavoured hosts)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Hosts have shipped on web-flavoured days (D24 jsp_webshell, D25 elixir_phoenix) and none on D23/D26. If zsh/fish ship, a host is likely a startup file: `.zshrc`/`.zshenv`/`.zprofile`, oh-my-zsh `*.plugin.zsh`, `~/.config/fish/config.fish`, `conf.d/*.fish`, autoload `functions/<name>.fish`, bash `.bashrc`/`.profile` (T1546.004 Unix shell configuration modification). Expected host_profile spellings follow `<platform>_<kind>` (guess list for fixtures only: `zsh_rc`, `oh_my_zsh_plugin`, `fish_config`) -- answers stay plan-verbatim. Fixtures: marker + descriptor inside a function/alias/`precmd` h