efine DESCRIPTOR`..`endef` and `$(info ..)`, Dockerfile `LABEL huntress.descriptor=\\\"..\\\"`, XSLT `<xsl:variable name=\\\"d\\\" select=\\\"'..'\\\"/>`, HCL `output \\\"plan\\\" { value = \\\"..\\\" }`. Test: same plan with and without the marker line. Must stay inside the 2 s find_codecs fixture budget (gate on cheap substring/length tests). D27 Dockerfile added the INDIRECT form: `ARG HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR=\\\"<data>\\\"` then `LABEL huntress.analysis.descriptor=$HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR` (the use site is a variable reference) -- the fallback must keep the literal, not the `$VAR` use. Re-try after 1 failed attempt; keep imports in hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"make-recipe-inner-scripts\", \"concept\": \"build-file recipes/RUN lines that embed PRIOR-language scripts (bash, PowerShell, Python, Node) as a handoff\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 Dockerfile shipped only FROM/ARG/LABEL, but the build-file theme invites `RUN` / recipe bodies carrying earlier languages: Dockerfile `RUN <<EOF ... EOF` heredocs, `RUN [\\\"pwsh\\\",\\\"-c\\\",\\\"..\\\"]` exec form, `SHELL [\\\"powershell\\\",\\\"-Command\\\"]`, `RUN echo <b64> | base64 -d | sh`; Makefile `SHELL := pwsh`, `.ONESHELL:` multi-line recipes, `$(shell python3 -c '..')`, `\\\\`-continued recipe lines, `@` / `-` prefixes. Prebuild lib.codec.build_inner_scripts(text) -> [(locus, language, script_text)] (Dockerfile instruction / make target, interpreter from SHELL or the command head, `$$` -> `$` unescaped), then route each inner script to the existing analysers (lib.codec.v3_plan / find_codecs). Fixtures: a marker+plan only inside a RUN heredoc and only inside a .ONESHELL recipe. Never docker build / make.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"specimen-lineage-attribution\", \"concept\": \"attribute specimens to their true parent when they share strings with others (D27 prompt; never asked yet)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 prompt: 'A Dockerfile and several earlier specimens share strings, but sharing strings doesn't mean sharing parents. Attribute each specimen using build-stage, semantic, and static-handoff evidence, and expose the resemblance that's only skin-deep.' Nothing shipped (14th narrative). cross-language-collision-decoys (built) flags look-alike indicators; this adds PARENT attribution: lib.codec.lineage(plans_by_member, texts_by_member) -> {member: (parent_member|None, evidence)} where evidence ranks (1) static handoff edges (producer next_stage/next_language/handoff_id == consumer member/language/HandoffId), (2) build-stage edges (Dockerfile `FROM x AS y`/`COPY --from=y`, make prerequisites), (3) semantic match (same campaign token AND same role chain), and only last (4) shared strings -- a 'skin-deep' member = shares url/host/path strings with A but its campaign token / handoff edge points to B. Per Mastery set. Answer shapes to expect: parent member file name, parent language, or the decoy member; new suffixes -> lib.codec.plan_answer first. Fixtures: 3 members sharing a url host, only one with a handoff edge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"terraform-hcl-v3-fixtures\", \"concept\": \"Terraform HCL v=3 polyglot in the exact D23-D27 shape (family with an underscore)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"terraform_hcl is in the 13 unshipped languages; terraform-hcl-function-fold (built) folds HCL functions. Add D27-shaped fixtures `polyglot-terraform_hcl-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}.tf`: line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` (also `//` and `/* */` variants), `locals { huntress_descriptor = \\\"..\\\" }`, `variable \\\"huntress_descriptor\\\" { default = \\\"..\\\" }`, heredoc `<<-EOT`..`EOT`, `output \\\"plan\\\" { value = local.huntress_descriptor }` (indirect use like D27 LABEL), `resource \\\"terraform_data\\\" \\\"analysis_<8hex>\\\" {}`. Assert family `polyglot-terraform_hcl`, campaign `TERRAFORM_HCL-<8hex>`, host `terraform_hcl-<10hex>.example.invalid` (underscore kept, like D17 auto_hotkey / D21 github_actions), /tmp/huntress-terraform_hcl/, longest-suffix id parse. Never terraform init/plan.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xslt-v3-fixtures\", \"concept\": \"XSLT v=3 polyglot in the exact D23-D27 shape (XML comment marker, xsl:variable descriptor)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"xslt is unshipped; xslt-msxsl-route (built) pulls msxsl:script bodies. Add D27-shaped fixtures `polyglot-xslt-*.xsl`: `<?xml ..?>` FIRST (so the marker is on line 2), `<!-- HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-.. -->`, `<xsl:variable name=\\\"huntress_descriptor\\\" select=\\\"'..'\\\"/>` / `<xsl:param>` / text content `<xsl:variable name=\\\"d\\\">..</xsl:variable>`, a use site `<xsl:value-of select=\\\"$huntress_descriptor\\\"/>`, data possibly entity-escaped (`&#x2E;` for FRAG dots) or in CDATA. Assert the marker regex stops at `-->` and that entity-decoded rescans work; plan-verbatim language=xslt, XSLT-<8hex>. Parse with xml.etree only (no DTD/entity expansion, never apply the stylesheet).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"build-file-host-profiles\", \"concept\": \"HOST profiles for build/infra files wrapping prior languages (compose, CMake, justfile, package.json scripts)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"No host shipped with D26 Erlang or D27 Dockerfile; if D28 (Makefile) brings one, it is likely a build-orchestration wrapper: docker-compose.yml `services: x: command:`/`entrypoint:`/`build: args:`, CMake `execute_process(COMMAND ..)`/`file(DOWNLOAD ..)`, justfile recipes, `package.json` `\\\"scripts\\\": {\\\"postinstall\\\": \\\"..\\\"}`, `Taskfile.yml` `cmds:`. Expected host_profile spelling `<tool>_<kind>` (fixture guesses only: `docker_compose`, `cmake_project`, `npm_lifecycle`) -- answers stay plan-verbatim; route by marker. Fixtures: marker + descriptor inside each wrapper (YAML scalar, JSON string with `\\\\\\\"` escapes, CMake `set(HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR \\\"..\\\")`). Stdlib only (json, a minimal YAML scalar reader -- no PyYAML `on:`->True surprises).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"v3-tag-vocab-extend\", \"concept\": \"new v=3 carrier TAG names in the single (beyond B64/HEX/HB64/FRAG/SPLIT/LYR)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The single has used B64/HEX/HB64/FRAG for 20 days and D27's timed dropped LYR again; a late-event twist may add a tag (B32, B85, ZB64 = zlib+b64, GZB64, ROT13, REV, UTF16B64, XOR<key>, URL). Prebuild a tag table in lib.codec (tag -> decode chain) with a shape-peel fallback for unknown tags (max 4 layers, zlib/gzip magic, base32 alphabet, utf-16le NUL pattern), and fixtures for each tag in a `#`, `//`, `%`, `<!-- -->` comment. The obfuscation answer has always been plan-verbatim (obfuscation_profile=) in the single -- assert the peel never invents it.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"shell-rc-host-carriers\", \"concept\": \"shell startup/config files as v=3 HOST profiles for zsh/fish/bash (persistence-flavoured hosts)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Hosts have shipped on web-flavoured days (D24 jsp_webshell, D25 elixir_phoenix) and none on D23/D26. If zsh/fish ship, a host is likely a startup file: `.zshrc`/`.zshenv`/`.zprofile`, oh-my-zsh `*.plugin.zsh`, `~/.config/fish/config.fish`, `conf.d/*.fish`, autoload `functions/<name>.fish`, bash `.bashrc`/`.profile` (T1546.004 Unix shell configuration modification). Expected host_profile spellings follow `<platform>_<kind>` (guess list for fixtures only: `zsh_rc`, `oh_my_zsh_plugin`, `fish_config`) -- answers stay plan-verbatim. Fixtures: marker + descriptor inside a function/alias/`precmd` hook, plus `source`/`autoload -Uz` lines that must be ignored. Assert routing by marker, not by file name. D27 Dockerfile came with NO host (4 of the last 5 languages: D23, D26, D27 none; D24/D25 web hosts) -- hosts only on web-flavoured days so far.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dockerfile-multistage-stage-graph\", \"concept\": \"multi-stage Dockerfile build graph (stage parents, COPY --from, ONBUILD) for build-stage attribution\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 shipped one `FROM scratch AS analysis_<8hex>` stage per file; the prompt's 'build-stage evidence' suggests multi-stage files could appear in a later cumulative/timed delivery. lib.codec.docker_stages(text) -> ordered [{name, base, args, labels, copies_from, runs}] handling `ARG` before the first FROM (global scope) vs per-stage ARG, `FROM ${BASE} AS x`, `COPY --from=<stage|index|image>`, `ONBUILD`, line continuations `\\\\` and the `# escape=` directive (backtick escape on Windows images), `--platform`, heredocs. Feed to specimen-lineage-attribution. Fixtures: 3-stage file where the plan is in stage 1 and LABELled in stage 3 via `COPY --from`.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"corpus-aggregate-questions\", \"concept\": \"final-days capstone questions over the whole cumulative corpus (counts, languages per role, handoff paths)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"With 4 days left the single holds ~1700 ids over ~175 members of 30+ languages; a capstone day could ask corpus-level questions (how many members per role, which language hands off to X, longest next_language chain, members sharing a campaign token, count of benign_utility). Prebuild lib.codec.corpus_summary(plans_by_member) -> dict of role/attack/language/next_language/host_profile counters, next_language edge list and its longest path, campaign-token groups; per Mastery set. Answer kinds to expect: integer, ordered_tokens (joined with `>`), exact_text member names. Fixtures from a synthetic 12-member corpus.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scope\", \"concept\": \"resolve every cross-file reference inside its own Mastery set\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery e24c070d: `4c1097.py` existed in all 7 sets; a bundle-wide index returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Index per inner evidence-0N.zip; cases must keep set-distinct values. D24: stems identical across all 8 sets again (`588efb.jsp` set1..set8) with set-distinct plans; the D23 per-set fix held (Mastery 2afec5c3 first try). D25: 9 sets, stems again identical across sets (`a7470f.exs` set1..set9); first try. D26 10 sets, D27 11 sets (semantic ids `setN.<lang>-<role>-<field>`); first try both days.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"timed-contract-shape-diff\", \"concept\": \"diff the timed contract's id grammar against the single's before trusting the carried solver\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: single = semantic ids, timed = per-file hashed ids + composite fields; answered/asked dropped to 593/1495 and cost ~25 min across TT+Mastery. A pre-run check (answered ratio < 0.98 on a fresh contract => generalize offline before submitting) would have caught it; workers must not inline the 1500-id contract (one generalize worker died at 1.39 M tokens). D24: the per-file grammar persisted unchanged (TT 1560 = 1495 + 65 jsp ids; 0 generalize workers); keep the check, it now guards the NEXT reshape. D25: unchanged a 3rd time (TT 1625 = 1560 + 65 elixir ids). D26: unchanged a 4th time (TT 1677). **D27: REVERTED to the single's semantic grammar** (TT 1659 = single, Mastery 11 x 1659 = 18249, no 6hex stems, no LYR tags, no colour_shape stage_profile, next_language only base languages); the carried solver handled it because it keeps both grammars. Never delete the semantic path when a reshape lands; expect a further flip either way on D28-D31.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"next-language-pool-roadmap\", \"concept\": \"forecast the next language: timed next_language pool (D24-D27) is GONE, fall back to sibling pairs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"4/4 hits while it lasted: D23 pool had jsp -> D24 JSP; elixir -> D25; erlang -> D26; dockerfile -> D27 Dockerfile. D27's timed contract reverted to the single shape and its plans' next_language values were only the 8 shipped base languages (bash, batch, javascript, jscript, php, powershell, python, vbscript), so there is no pool to read for D28. 13 unshipped (4 days left, D28-D31): awk, beanshell, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh. Consecutive drops paired by family twice (D25 Elixir -> D26 Erlang; D27 Dockerfile -> D28 Makefile?); remaining pairs zsh/fish, awk/sed, kotlin/beanshell. Still re-check today's auto-* expected.json `-next-language` values nightly in case the pool returns (only the cases harvested TODAY -- older cases carry stale pools).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OPEN after D27: the D27 solve.py (byte-identical D23/D24 copy) has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20-D22 needed none because every carrier was plain). Do it in the next solver-authoring pass.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd .jsp .exs (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .bsh .erl .ex .exs .nim .swift .fish .zsh .ipynb .go .rs .awk .tf .xsl .reg .inf .iss .wxs). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page). D20: `polyglot-groovy` (campaign GROOVY-), hosts `host-jenkins-pipeline-groovy` (profile jenkins_pipeline) and `host-classic-asp-vbscript` (profile classic_asp, language vbscript, campaign VBSCRIPT-, file .vbs although the bytes are an ASP page). D21: `polyglot-github_actions` (campaign GITHUB_ACTIONS-, url host github_actions-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-github_actions/..), no host file. D22: `polyglot-nsis` (campaign NSIS-, url host nsis-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-nsis/..), no host file. D24: `polyglot-jsp` (campaign JSP-, url host jsp-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-jsp/..) + host `host-jsp-webshell-jsp` (profile jsp_webshell); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-jsp` (5 members). D25: `polyglot-elixir` (campaign ELIXIR-, url host elixir-.., /tmp/huntress-elixir/) + host `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir` (profile elixir_phoenix); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-elixir` (5 members). D26: `polyglot-erlang` (ERLANG-), no host. D27: `polyglot-dockerfile` (campaign DOCKERFILE-, url host dockerfile-.., /tmp/huntress-dockerfile/), no host; a terraform_hcl day would bring `polyglot-terraform_hcl` (underscore, TERRAFORM_HCL-).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"godot-re-tools\", \"concept\": \"Godot pack/bytecode extractor\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"gdsdecomp (GDRE Tools) release binary into tools/gdre (headless: `gdre_tools --headless --recover=x.pck --output-dir=out`); only for .pck/.gdc/.exe Godot exports; never run the game. Static lib reader (godot-resource-pck-carrier) covers plain packs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"unrpyc\", \"concept\": \"Ren'Py .rpyc decompiler\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/CensoredUsername/unrpyc into tools/unrpyc; it unpickles (code execution risk) -- run only under python3 -I in the sandbox on copies, prefer the restricted lib reader.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"}\n]\n```","numLines":113,"startLine":186,"totalLines":299}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CxWq64k3nHFBFkPhzMmEak","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
