{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgUh5Bvner38JrLieBj7W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Us7jC7JkbRPWcwHypJBXWi","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/script-analysis.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\")\nold=json.loads(s[s.index(\"```json\",i)+7:s.rindex(\"```\")])\nkeep={g['id']:g for g in old}\nprose=\"\"\"## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D26 nights (see git history) and D27 night\nmakefile-v3-carrier-forms, var-interpolation-concat-fold, function-return-literal-battery, specimen-lineage-attribution,\nterraform-hcl-v3-fixtures, xslt-v3-fixtures, build-file-host-profiles, v3-tag-vocab-extend, shell-rc-host-carriers,\ndockerfile-multistage-stage-graph, corpus-aggregate-questions. Every one of the 12 pool languages now has single-shape fixtures\n(zsh/fish, awk/sed, nim/swift/tcl, kotlin/beanshell, makefile, xslt, rust). Given up (2 attempts): python-exec-onion-static,\nevidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile, macos-pkg-installer-scripts, zsh-fish-shell-route,\nawk-sed-program-route, composite-label-field-regime. Prebuild rules learned: only hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (no\n`__import__`, no `tomllib`); keep fixtures tiny (other lanes' slow fixtures under load have sunk script-lane attempts).\nPriority-1 order for D29: 12 pool languages / 3 days -> a MULTI-language drop through the carried solver in BOTH timed grammars\n(the D28 per-file flip landed new families straight into `<6hex>` ids + LYR), then a prior-language script embedded inside the\nnew file (the D28 prompt's \"prior scripts and relationship evidence\"); then LYR vocabulary, pool-language hosts, decode-call\nwrappers, make recipes; the D28 \"out of order\" narrative readers last.\n\n\"\"\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"multi-language-drop-battery\",\"concept\":\"2-4 never-shipped pool languages landing on ONE day, answered end-to-end by the carried solver in both timed grammars\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 left 12 pool languages (awk, beanshell, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, xslt, zsh) for 3 days (D29-D31): a multi-language day is likely. Per-language single-shape fixtures exist (built D23-D27 nights) but nothing runs a whole CONTRACT. Prebuild a synthetic case generator + fixtures: 3 new families in the D28 layout (line-1 `<comment> HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>`, a header block, a named `huntress_descriptor_<8hex>` literal, an indirect use like D28 `output { value = local.x }` / D27 `LABEL ..=$X`), rendered as (a) a semantic contract (`polyglot-<lang>-<role>-<field>`, 11 fields) and (b) a per-file contract (`polyglot-<lang>-<6hex>-<field>`, 13 fields incl. url-host/path-leaf/campaign-token, LYR-tagged markers). Assert 100% answered by lib.codec.v3_plan + plan_answer for underscore-free and underscore families, campaign-token = after the FIRST hyphen (`TERRAFORM_HCL-10a06eec` -> `10a06eec`), url-host keeps `_`. Stdlib only; tiny fixtures.\"},\n {\"id\":\"embedded-prior-script-dual-plan\",\"concept\":\"a new-language file that embeds a PRIOR-language fixture (its own Codec_/v=1-2 plan) next to its own v=3 marker\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 prompt: 'Assemble the timeline from resources, prior scripts, and relationship evidence' -- prior scripts were never embedded yet, but D19 ASPX already nested a whole inner file. Expect e.g. Terraform `provisioner \\\"local-exec\\\" { command = <<-EOT .. EOT }` / Makefile recipe / Kotlin raw string `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` / XSLT CDATA / fish `begin; ..; end` holding a PowerShell/bash/batch fixture with `Codec_<id>`/`Material_<id>`. Prebuild lib.codec.embedded_scripts(text) -> [(locus, language_guess, inner_text)] (heredoc/raw-string/CDATA/escaped-string extraction, unescape `\\\\n \\\\\\\" $$ &quot;`), and a selector: the OUTER file's v=3 marker plan answers its polyglot ids; inner plans are returned separately for new suffixes (`-inner-*`, `-prior-*`, `-next-stage`) via plan_answer. Fixtures: same file with outer B64 marker + inner PS FromBase64String descriptor + inner bash Codec_; assert the outer plan is never replaced by the inner one.\"},\n {\"id\":\"lyr-layer-vocab-extend\",\"concept\":\"timed LYR-<layers> tags with layer names beyond b64/b32/hex/rev/frag\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 timed brought LYR back (1-3 layers of b64/b32/hex/rev/frag, encode order, obfuscation answer = the layer string verbatim, e.g. `b32_rev_b64`). v3-tag-vocab-extend (built) covers SINGLE tags only. A late twist could add layers (`b85`/`a85`, `z`/`zlib`, `gz`, `rot13`, `url`, `u16`, `xor<hex>`, 4+ deep). Prebuild: extend the tag-directed peel with a layer table + shape-peel fallback for an unknown layer name (try each known decoder at that position, accept only a final `v=`), and keep the obfuscation answer = the raw tag text. Fixtures for each new layer in `#`, `//`, `--`, `<!-- -->`, `%` comments, 4-deep stacks; must stay inside the 2 s budget.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pool-language-host-wrappers\",\"concept\":\"HOST profiles for the remaining pool languages (Gradle, JMeter BeanShell, Package.swift, nimble, Expect, wmic XSL)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Hosts shipped only on web-flavoured days (D24 jsp_webshell, D25 elixir_phoenix); D26-D28 had none. If a pool language brings one, likely wrappers: Kotlin `build.gradle.kts` (`tasks.register(\\\"x\\\") { doLast { .. } }`), BeanShell inside a JMeter `.jmx` (XML-escaped `<stringProp name=\\\"BeanShellSampler.query\\\">` -> NESTED carrier with `&quot;`/`&#xa;`), Swift `Package.swift`, Nim `.nimble` tasks, Tcl `expect` script, XSLT run by `wmic os get /format:` (Squiblytwo), zsh/fish rc files (built: shell-rc-host-carriers). host_profile spellings follow `<tool>_<kind>` (fixture guesses only: gradle_build, jmeter_beanshell, swift_package, wmic_xsl) -- answers stay plan-verbatim; route by marker. Fixtures: marker + descriptor inside each wrapper incl. one XML-entity-escaped JMX; assert lib.codec.v3_plan unescapes and rescans.\"},\n {\"id\":\"descriptor-decode-call-wrapper\",\"concept\":\"descriptor literal wrapped in the host language's own decode call (marker kept or dropped)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D27/D28 split declaration from use; the next step is the literal inside a decode expression: HCL `base64decode(\\\"..\\\")`/`jsondecode`, Kotlin/BeanShell `String(Base64.getDecoder().decode(\\\"..\\\"))`, Swift `Data(base64Encoded: \\\"..\\\")`, Nim `decode(\\\"..\\\")` (std/base64), Rust `STANDARD.decode(\\\"..\\\")`, Tcl `binary decode base64 {..}`, zsh/fish `$(print -r -- .. | base64 -d)` / `echo .. | base64 -d`, XSLT none. Prebuild in lib.codec: recognise these call shapes, take the argument literal, apply the named decode before the shape peel (count it as a layer), accept only `v=`. Fixtures with and without the line-1 marker; assert the marker plan wins when both exist.\"},\n {\"id\":\"change-order-anomaly\",\"concept\":\"'find the change that happened out of order' -- ordering anomalies over plans/handoffs (D28 prompt; never asked)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 prompt asked to 'assemble the timeline ... and find the change that happened out of order'; nothing shipped (15th narrative). If a question comes, the evidence in the corpus is: plan `steps` order vs the canonical role order (acquire_remote before dispatch_*, decode_* before write_file before dispatch_process), stage_count vs len(steps), next_language/next_stage handoff edges vs member order, and any timestamps (zip member mtimes -- all fixed 2026-01-01 so far -- or plan keys like `created=`/`seq=`). Prebuild lib.codec.order_anomalies(plans_by_member, zip_infos=None) -> [(member, kind, evidence)] per Mastery set; 